<title>HONG KONG: Wheelock seen eyeing HK$3.0 bln loan.</title>
<headline>Wheelock seen eyeing HK$3.0 bln loan.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wheelock and Co is seeking a HK$3.0 billion revolving credit/term loan facility, bankers said.</p>
<p>The loan matures in three years but can be extended at the borrower's option to five years, they said.</p>
<p>The loan reportedly pays a margin of 50 basis points over the Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate and an all-in return of 62.5 basis points to top tier participants.</p>
<p>ABN Amro, Chase Manhattan Asia and Hang Seng Bank are arrangers, bankers said</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
